. * nwsbm tutorial 1: a stochastic block model for the karate club
. * Requires the core nwcommands and the package nwsbm. The data (Zachary 1977) ar
> e loaded from the nwcommands website.
. set linesize 80

. 
. nwwebuse zachary, nwclear

. nwsummarize zachary_bin
--------------------------------------------------
   Network name:  zachary_bin
   Network id:  1
   Directed: false
   Valued: false
   Two-mode: false
   Nodes: 34
   Selfloop: false
   Edges: 78
   Minimum value:  0
   Maximum value:  1
   Density:  .139
   Mean degree:  4.59
   Temporal: false

. 
. * --- fit block models with one to five blocks and select the number of blocks
>  by the ICL ---
. nwsbm zachary_bin, maxblocks(5) seed(20261120) generate(block) replace

Stochastic block model (bernoulli, undirected)             Actors    =        34
Network: zachary_bin                                       Blocks    =         2
                                                           ICL       =   -206.06
                                                           Lower bound J=   -193
> .95

--------------------------------------------------------------
      Blocks |         ICL           J          PL  parameters
-------------+------------------------------------------------
          1  |     -229.37     -226.20     -226.20           1
          2* |     -206.06     -193.95     -194.80           3
          3  |     -216.63     -189.07     -194.11           6
          4  |     -218.32     -177.58     -181.38          10
          5  |     -230.01     -171.03     -175.49          15
--------------------------------------------------------------
* selected by the largest ICL

Block sizes:

    b1  b2
r1  29   5
Block proportions:

        b1      b2
r1  0.8517  0.1483
Block connectivity, tie probability, from the row block to the column block:

        b1      b2
b1  0.0476
b2  0.3680  0.4937

. 
. * --- the model selection table again, and the blocks ---
. estat icl

Model selection by the integrated classification likelihood (ICL), bernoulli mod
> el
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
      Blocks |          ICL           J          PL           H  parameters
-------------+--------------------------------------------------------------
          1  |      -229.37     -226.20     -226.20        0.00           1
          2* |      -206.06     -193.95     -194.80        0.85           3
          3  |      -216.63     -189.07     -194.11        5.05           6
          4  |      -218.32     -177.58     -181.38        3.80          10
          5  |      -230.01     -171.03     -175.49        4.46          15
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* selected by the largest ICL (ties within 1e-9: fewest blocks)

. estat blocks

Blocks
---------------------------------------------
  Block |      Size  Proportion        Within
--------+------------------------------------
      1 |        29      0.8517        0.0476
      2 |         5      0.1483        0.4937
---------------------------------------------
Within: connectivity within the block (the diagonal of the connectivity matrix).

. 
. * --- plots: blocked adjacency matrix, block graph, ICL curve, memberships ---
. nwsbmplot, type(matrix) shade export(nwsbm1_matrix.png)

. nwsbmplot, type(blocks) export(nwsbm1_blocks.png)

. nwsbmplot, type(icl) export(nwsbm1_icl.png)

. nwsbmplot, type(membership) export(nwsbm1_membership.png)

. 
. * --- how do the blocks relate to the two factions of the club? ---
. tabulate block group

     nwsbm |
     block |         group
     (MAP) |         1          2 |     Total
-----------+----------------------+----------
         1 |        13         16 |        29 
         2 |         3          2 |         5 
-----------+----------------------+----------
     Total |        16         18 |        34 

. 
. * --- force three blocks ---
. nwsbm zachary_bin, blocks(3) seed(20261120) generate(block3) replace

